
                                                         Changes


Changes with nginx 1.29.3                                        12 Dec 2025

    *) Feature: centralized HTTP status code registry and validation API.

       This release introduces a unified HTTP status code management system
       with RFC 9110 compliance validation. The new architecture includes:

       - Centralized status code registry with reason phrases and metadata
       - ngx_http_status_set() API for validated status code assignment
       - ngx_http_status_validate() for RFC 9110 range validation
       - ngx_http_status_reason() for standard reason phrase lookup
       - ngx_http_status_is_cacheable() for RFC 9111 cache decisions
       - Optional strict validation via --with-http_status_validation flag

       The refactoring maintains full backward compatibility with existing
       nginx.conf configurations and third-party modules. All status code
       assignments now route through the unified API while preserving
       upstream pass-through semantics for proxied responses.

       Status flags: NGX_HTTP_STATUS_CACHEABLE, NGX_HTTP_STATUS_CLIENT_ERROR,
       NGX_HTTP_STATUS_SERVER_ERROR, NGX_HTTP_STATUS_INFORMATIONAL.

       Build option: --with-http_status_validation enables strict RFC 9110
       compliance checking including reserved code detection (306) and
       warnings for non-standard NGINX-specific codes (444, 494-499).

